                <pb facs="0361" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.6511/1364a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-30">March 30, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>821. Bequest Foreign Office inform appropriate Governments that within next few
                    days Italian, Hungarian and Bulgarian official groups will be moved to Grove
                    Park Inn, Asheville, North Carolina, and Japanese official group to Greenbrier
                    Hotel, White Sulphur Springs, West Virginia and that new accommodations will be
                    equal to those presently enjoyed by personnel concerned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
